# Command line

`nml` has four commands. `nml help <command>` describes each.

## nml init {#init}

```sh
nml init [root]
```

Makes `root`, the current directory by default, a workspace: writes an `nml.toml` if there is none, and in `.nml/` the declarations of the Lua API and the sources of the standard library, for editors.

## nml build {#build}

```sh
nml build [root]
nml build file.nml [--output page.html]
```

Builds the workspace at `root`, the current directory by default: see [[building#]]. With a file instead, builds that one file without a workspace, next to it or to `--output`. Fails if there are errors. Errors are in color on a terminal.

## nml serve {#serve}

```sh
nml serve [root] [--port 8080] [--open]
```

Serves the workspace's pages at `http://127.0.0.1:<port>`, a free port by default, and opens the browser with `--open`. It watches the workspace: on each saved change, it builds again — without writing the output — and the pages in the browser follow. Errors are printed as they come. It stops with `Ctrl-C`.

## nml lsp {#lsp}

```sh
nml lsp
```

Runs the language server on standard input and output, for [[editors#|editors]].

## Environment

| Variable | |
|:---------|:-|
| `NML_LUALS` | Where the language server finds [LuaLS](https://luals.github.io). |
| `SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH` | The time scripts see, for [[building#reproducible|reproducible builds]]. |
